 7965              		.file 5 "../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h"
   1:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h **** /**
   2:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *  Core bignum functions
   3:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *
   4:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *  This interface should only be used by the legacy bignum module (bignum.h)
   5:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *  and the modular bignum modules (bignum_mod.c, bignum_mod_raw.c). All other
   6:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *  modules should use the high-level modular bignum interface (bignum_mod.h)
   7:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *  or the legacy bignum interface (bignum.h).
   8:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *
   9:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * This module is about processing non-negative integers with a fixed upper
  10:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * bound that's of the form 2^n-1 where n is a multiple of #biL.
  11:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * These can be thought of integers written in base 2^#biL with a fixed
  12:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * number of digits. Digits in this base are called *limbs*.
  13:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * Many operations treat these numbers as the principal representation of
  14:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * a number modulo 2^n or a smaller bound.
  15:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *
  16:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * The functions in this module obey the following conventions unless
  17:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * explicitly indicated otherwise:
  18:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *
  19:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Overflow**: some functions indicate overflow from the range
  20:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   [0, 2^n-1] by returning carry parameters, while others operate
  21:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   modulo and so cannot overflow. This should be clear from the function
  22:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   documentation.
  23:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Bignum parameters**: Bignums are passed as pointers to an array of
  24:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   limbs. A limb has the type #mbedtls_mpi_uint. Unless otherwise specified:
  25:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *     - Bignum parameters called \p A, \p B, ... are inputs, and are
  26:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *       not modified by the function.
  27:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *     - For operations modulo some number, the modulus is called \p N
  28:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *       and is input-only.
  29:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *     - Bignum parameters called \p X, \p Y are outputs or input-output.
  30:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *       The initial content of output-only parameters is ignored.
GAS LISTING /tmp/ccpAd290.s 			page 254


  31:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *     - Some functions use different names that reflect traditional
  32:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *       naming of operands of certain operations (e.g.
  33:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *       divisor/dividend/quotient/remainder).
  34:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *     - \p T is a temporary storage area. The initial content of such
  35:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *       parameter is ignored and the final content is unspecified.
  36:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Bignum sizes**: bignum sizes are always expressed in limbs.
  37:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   Most functions work on bignums of a given size and take a single
  38:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   \p limbs parameter that applies to all parameters that are limb arrays.
  39:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   All bignum sizes must be at least 1 and must be significantly less than
  40:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   #SIZE_MAX. The behavior if a size is 0 is undefined. The behavior if the
  41:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   total size of all parameters overflows #SIZE_MAX is undefined.
  42:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Parameter ordering**: for bignum parameters, outputs come before inputs.
  43:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   Temporaries come last.
  44:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Aliasing**: in general, output bignums may be aliased to one or more
  45:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   inputs. As an exception, parameters that are documented as a modulus value
  46:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   may not be aliased to an output. Outputs may not be aliased to one another.
  47:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   Temporaries may not be aliased to any other parameter.
  48:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Overlap**: apart from aliasing of limb array pointers (where two
  49:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   arguments are equal pointers), overlap is not supported and may result
  50:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   in undefined behavior.
  51:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Error handling**: This is a low-level module. Functions generally do not
  52:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   try to protect against invalid arguments such as nonsensical sizes or
  53:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   null pointers. Note that some functions that operate on bignums of
  54:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   different sizes have constraints about their size, and violating those
  55:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   constraints may lead to buffer overflows.
  56:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  * - **Modular representatives**: functions that operate modulo \p N expect
  57:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   all modular inputs to be in the range [0, \p N - 1] and guarantee outputs
  58:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   in the range [0, \p N - 1]. If an input is out of range, outputs are
  59:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   fully unspecified, though bignum values out of range should not cause
  60:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *   buffer overflows (beware that this is not extensively tested).
  61:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  */
  62:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h **** 
  63:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h **** /*
  64:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/bignum_core.h ****  *  Copyright The Mbed TLS Contributors
